10
00:39:13,846 --> 00:39:19,846
Paddler (voice), played by Matt Berry.

11
00:43:09,230 --> 00:43:15,230
The Wild Robot is a 2024 American animated science fiction film based on the
2016 novel by Peter Brown and produced by DreamWorks Animation.

12
00:47:04,615 --> 00:47:10,615
It was written and directed by Chris Sanders and features the voices of Lupita Nyong'o, Pedro Pascal, Kit
Connor, Bill Nighy, Stephanie Hsu, Matt Berry, Ving Rhames, Mark Hamill, and Catherine O'Hara.

13
00:51:00,000 --> 00:51:06,000
The film follows a service robot shipwrecked on an island who must adapt to her surroundings, build
relationships with the local wildlife, and become the adoptive mother of an orphaned goose.

14
00:54:55,384 --> 00:55:01,384
DreamWorks Animation bought the screenplay before
the first novel's release in 2016.

15
00:58:50,769 --> 00:58:56,769
Sanders first encountered the original book through his daughter and was
offered an opportunity to direct a film adaptation at DreamWorks.

16
01:02:46,153 --> 01:02:52,153
The film's visuals use a watercolor aesthetic, inspired by classic
Disney animated films and the works of Hayao Miyazaki.

17
01:06:41,538 --> 01:06:47,538
Kris Bowers composed the score, marking his first
score for a fully animated film.

18
01:10:36,923 --> 01:10:42,923
Development took four years on a budget of $78 million.

19
01:14:32,307 --> 01:14:38,307
The Wild Robot premiered at the 49th Toronto International Film Festival on September 8, 2024,
and was released in the United States on September 27, by Universal Pictures.

20
01:18:27,692 --> 01:18:33,692
The film received critical acclaim from critics who praised it for its
writing, animation, score, emotional depth, and voice acting.

21
01:22:23,076 --> 01:22:29,076
The film was a commercial success, grossing $334.5 million worldwide.

22
01:26:18,461 --> 01:26:24,461
Among its accolades, it received nine Annie Awards (including Best Animated Feature), won Best Animated Feature at the Critics' Choice Awards and Producers Guild of
America Awards, and was nominated for four Golden Globe Awards and three Academy Awards, becoming DreamWorks' most-nominated film at the latter ceremony.

23
01:30:13,846 --> 01:30:19,846
A sequel is in development.

24
01:34:09,230 --> 01:34:15,230
The film explores themes of villain, robot, based on
children's book, female villain, aftercreditsstinger.

25
01:38:04,615 --> 01:38:10,615
The tone is lighthearted and emotional and thought_provoking.
